This log text is five lines, held in the program as one string literal with
embedded newlines:

    2026-01-01 INFO start
    2026-01-02 WARN slow
    2026-01-03 INFO done
    2026-01-04 ERROR crash
    2026-01-05 INFO ok

Each line carries exactly one severity word: INFO, WARN, or ERROR. Extract
every severity word with a single regular expression, then print three lines:

1. how many severity words were found
2. how many of them are INFO
3. the distinct severity words in ascending order, joined into one string
   with a comma between them and no spaces

Print each with `.` followed by `cr`, so each line holds one value.
